===Etymology 2===
Alteration of ''[[well]]'' (verb), probably influenced by the past participle.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To bind together [[inseparably]]; to [[unite]] closely or [[intimately]].
# {{transitive}} To [[join]] two [[material]]s (especially two [[metal]]s) together by applying [[heat]], [[pressure]] and [[filler]], either separately or in any combination.

=====Quotations=====
* '''1847''': [[w:Alfred Lord Tennyson|Alfred Lord Tennyson]], ''The Princess''
*: Now should men see / Two women faster '''welded''' in one love / Than pairs of wedlock.

